    "q-183353": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183353",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Which of the following is **NOT** a grammatical construction for the biconditional $P⇔Q?$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the biconditional $P⇔Q:$\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ iff $Q$\n\n- $P$ is necessary and sufficient for $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and conversely\n\nFrom the given options, the only one that is NOT a grammatical construction for $P⇔Q$ is \"$P$ is sufficient for $Q$\" (this is the grammatical construction of $P⇒Q).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
